>> title: Apple Crisp
>> servings: 8
>> source: https://www.thechunkychef.com/old-fashioned-easy-apple-crisp/#wprm-recipe-container-11755

Preheat oven to 350F. Lightly grease an #baking dish{8 x 8 inch}.

In a #medium bowl{2}, toss @apples{6}(peeled and sliced) with with @granulated sugar{2%tbsp}, @cinnamon{1%tsp}, and @lemon juice{1.5%tsp}. Transfer into the prepared baking dish and spread evenly.

In another medium bowl, combine @oats{0.75%cup}, @flour{0.75%cup}, @brown sugar{1%cup}, @cinnamon{1%tsp}, and @salt{pinch}. Cut in @cold butter{0.5%cups}(cubed) using a #fork{} or your fingers until the mixture turns into pea-sized crumbs.

Evenly sprinkle topping over the apple mixture in the baking dish. Bake for ~{40%minutes} until top is golden bwon and apples are tender and bubbling.